Template: homelab-mailread/db_host
Type: string
Default: localhost
Description: PostgreSQL host for the dovecot.users table:

Template: homelab-mailread/db_port
Type: string
Default: 5432
Description: PostgreSQL port:

Template: homelab-mailread/db_name
Type: string
Default: mailserver
Description: PostgreSQL database name:

Template: homelab-mailread/db_user
Type: string
Default: dovecot_user
Description: PostgreSQL role to connect as:

Template: homelab-mailread/db_password
Type: password
Description: PostgreSQL role password:

Template: homelab-mailread/maildir_base_path
Type: string
Default: /var/mail/vhosts
Description: Base path for Maildir storage:
 Mailboxes are stored at <base>/<domain>/<username>, owned by a vmail
 system user (UID/GID 5000, created if absent, matching production).

Template: homelab-mailread/introspection_url
Type: string
Default: https://api.mailmasker.org/api/v1/auth/introspect
Description: homelab-api JWT introspection URL (for the OAuth2 passdb):

Template: homelab-mailread/behind_proxy
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Is this host fronted by HAProxy (PROXY protocol)?
 Enable only if a homelab-mail-proxy (or equivalent) HAProxy instance
 terminates PROXY protocol in front of this host's IMAP/IMAPS listeners.
 Leave disabled for a standalone/test install.

Template: homelab-mailread/expose_sasl_auth_inet
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Expose the SASL auth service on a TCP port (12345) for a remote Postfix?
 Enable only if homelab-mailsend runs on a DIFFERENT host and needs
 cross-host SASL delegation (matching current production topology).
 Leave disabled if Postfix is co-located on this same host, or absent.

Template: homelab-mailread/sieve_global_script_path
Type: string
Default:
Description: Path to a global pre-delivery Sieve script (optional):
 Leave blank for none.

Template: homelab-mailread/force_overwrite_detected_config
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Existing hand-configured Dovecot SQL/OAuth2 auth was detected -- overwrite anyway?
 Decline (recommended on an already-hand-configured host) to install this
 package's config as *.recommended files alongside the running
 hand-configured setup instead of activating them.
